# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/SsvcDecisionType/trackStar node1259
node1259 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>trackStar</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/SsvcDecisionType/trackStar' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/SsvcDecisionType/trackStar</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;(&quot;Track\*&quot; in the SSVC spec) The vulnerability contains specific characteristics that may require closer monitoring for changes. CISA recommends remediating Track\* vulnerabilities within standard update timelines.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;(&quot;Track\*&quot; in the SSVC spec) The vulnerability contains specific characteristics that may require closer monitoring for changes. CISA recommends remediating Track\* vulnerabilities within standard update timelines.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/hasDataFile node1260
node1260 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>hasDataFile</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/hasDataFile' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/hasDataFile</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;The from Element treats each to Element as a data file. A data file is an artifact that stores data required or optional for the from Element&#x27;s functionality. A data file can be a database file, an index file, a log file, an AI model file, a calibration data file, a temporary file, a backup file, and more. For AI training dataset, test dataset, test artifact, configuration data, build input data, and build output data, please consider using the more specific relationship types: trainedOn, testedOn, hasTest, configures, hasInput, and hasOutput, respectively. This relationship does not imply dependency.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;The from Element treats each to Element as a data file. A data file is an artifact that stores data required or optional for the from Element&#x27;s functionality. A data file can be a database file, an index file, a log file, an AI model file, a calibration data file, a temporary file, a backup file, and more. For AI training dataset, test dataset, test artifact, configuration data, build input data, and build output data, please consider using the more specific relationship types: trainedOn, testedOn, hasTest, configures, hasInput, and hasOutput, respectively. This relationship does not imply dependency.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
